  "goodToKnow": "Das Grundwasser is groundwater. In Germany, about 70 percent of drinking water comes from it. Dry summers since 2018 have lowered the Grundwasserspiegel (water table) in many regions. Nitrate pollution from farming (Gülle, liquid manure) led the EU to take Germany to court, and it lost in 2018. The water is still strictly tested and safe to drink. It has no plural."
